# Known-harness fatal-diagnostic allowlist for scripts/run-gd-tests.sh
# running cad's suites. One extended-regex pattern per line, matched against
# composite records of the form
#
#     <diagnostic line> @@ <its `at:` location line>
#
# built from each suite's captured output. Every `SCRIPT ERROR:` and
# `ERROR: Failed to load script` record that matches NO pattern here FAILS
# the suite that printed it, even when its Results line is green. So each
# entry is a claim: "this diagnostic is the HOST HARNESS's, not the suite's"
# — and each needs its proof written next to it. A pattern added to silence a
# red run is the same act as deleting the assertion that failed.
#
# The file must contain at least one pattern. An allowlist of only comments
# is refused by the runner rather than treated as "nothing allowlisted":
# GNU grep reads an EMPTY -f pattern file as matching every line, so a
# pattern-less allowlist would filter out all diagnostics and silently
# disarm the entire check — the exact fail-open the layer exists to prevent.
#
# THE DOUBLE-LOAD QUIRK the compile-noise entries stem from: godot
# --headless --script <suite.gd> loads the script TWICE. The first load
# happens before the host project's autoloads register, so any script in the
# preload chain that names SingletonObject fails to compile, cascading
# "Failed to compile depended scripts." records up through the suite file,
# ending in one "Failed to load script ... with error 'Compilation failed'".
# The second load, after autoloads register, succeeds. A suite that is
# GENUINELY broken fails both loads and never prints a Results line, which
# the runner's Results floor already fails — so these patterns can never
# bless a suite that did not actually run.

# -- double-load pass-1 compile noise -----------------------------------------
# Pinned to the autoload name AND to host-side scripts (res://Scripts/) — an
# "Identifier not found" for anything else, or at a plugin/test path, is a
# real defect and must fail.
^SCRIPT ERROR: Compile Error: Identifier not found: SingletonObject @@ at: GDScript::reload \(res://Scripts/

# The cascade ("this script failed because a dependency did"). Location is
# deliberately unpinned: the cascade legitimately walks through the suite
# file itself. Safe because a cascade NEVER appears without its root-cause
# record, and only the SingletonObject root above is blessed — any other root
# (a Parse Error in a suite, an unknown identifier in a panel script) still
# fails on its own record.
^SCRIPT ERROR: Compile Error: Failed to compile depended scripts\. @@ at: GDScript::reload \(

# The pass-1 terminal record. Only the "Compilation failed" flavor is
# blessed — 'with error "Parse error"' (what a genuinely unparseable suite
# prints) is NOT.
^ERROR: Failed to load script ".*" with error "Compilation failed"\. @@ at: load \(modules/gdscript/gdscript\.cpp:

# -- headless-host startup noise ----------------------------------------------
# SingletonObject.initialize_plugins tries to .new() plugin scripts that do
# not compile in the headless host (other installed plugins' UI scripts) —
# host startup noise present in every suite's log regardless of what the
# suite does. Pinned to the exact function+file.
^SCRIPT ERROR: Invalid call\. Nonexistent function 'new' in base 'GDScript'\. @@ at: initialize_plugins \(res://Scripts/Models/singleton_object\.gd:
